  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "50d18a43-78e6-4844-a8b5-d8ae8abf6c98",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -4640,
        688
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 888,
        "height": 652,
        "content": "## 💰 SaaS Subscription Audit & Auto-Cancel Unused Seats\n\n### How it works\nEvery week, the workflow reads your subscription inventory from Google Sheets and loops through each seat. Per-platform HTTP calls fetch real usage data — Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, or a generic SaaS API. A code node normalises the raw responses into a uniform structure, then GPT-4o-mini assesses whether the seat is unused and what action to take. Unused seats trigger a cost-threshold check: high-cost seats (above a configurable dollar threshold) require a Slack approval before cancellation — the workflow waits for a manager to approve or reject via inline button. Low-cost unused seats are cancelled directly without asking. Every decision — active, cancelled, or rejected — is logged to the Audit Log sheet. After all seats are processed, a Slack summary report is posted with the run totals.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** and create a sheet with tabs: `Subscriptions`, `Audit Log`. Replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID` in all four Sheets nodes.\n2. Connect **OpenAI API** to the AI assessment node.\n3. Connect **Slack OAuth2** and replace `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID` in the approval request, summary, and error nodes.\n4. Add real API credentials and endpoints to the four platform usage nodes (Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, Generic).\n5. Set the high-cost threshold in the Is High Cost Seat? node to match your policy.\n6. Activate the weekly schedule trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "675c9bcf-a7f0-4532-b4d8-8b439b0ca8fe",
      "name": "Section – Weekly Trigger & Inventory",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3376,
        1264
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 472,
        "content": "## ⏰ Weekly Trigger & Subscription Inventory\nFires on a weekly schedule. Reads all active seat records from the Subscriptions sheet and feeds them into a loop — each seat is evaluated independently through the rest of the pipeline."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "86ebe0e2-1382-4a43-967c-c1714beb7363",
      "name": "Section – AI Usage Assessment",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1072,
        1136
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 984,
        "height": 552,
        "content": "## 🤖 AI Usage Assessment\nGPT-4o-mini receives the normalised seat data — platform, user, cost, days since last active — and returns a structured decision: `isUnused` (true/false), `recommendation` (cancel, keep, or escalate), and a plain-English reasoning note."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5736834e-0517-48bf-816d-2854ad5f901f",
      "name": "Section – Approval Flow & Cancellation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -16,
        1008
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1744,
        "height": 1560,
        "content": "## ✅ Approval Flow & Seat Cancellation\nHigh-cost unused seats require manager approval via a Slack inline button — the workflow waits indefinitely until a response arrives. Approved seats are cancelled via API and logged. Rejected seats are logged as overridden. Low-cost unused seats are cancelled directly without waiting for approval."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c3f3f81d-a34d-4e48-9501-5f233ab36fe6",
      "name": "Section – Run Summary & Error Handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2256,
        2640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1492,
        "height": 504,
        "content": "## 📊 Run Summary & Error Handling\nAfter all seats complete, a code node aggregates the totals — active, cancelled, rejected — and posts a Slack summary. A global error trigger catches any node failure and posts a structured Slack alert."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "bcbbd9fd-258d-410e-929a-442fc24de0e1",
      "name": "🔑 Credentials & Security",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1856,
        2352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 338,
        "content": "## 🔑 Credentials Required\n- **Google Sheets OAuth2** — Subscriptions + Audit Log\n- **OpenAI API** — seat usage assessment\n- **Slack OAuth2** — approval requests, summary, error alerts\n- **Platform APIs** — Google Workspace Admin, Slack, Zoom, custom SaaS\n\nNever hardcode API keys or personal emails in shared templates."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
